    "q-140366": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140366",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{4},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We require a $4\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-4)x+5y+(-1)z \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+7z \\\\ (-6)x+1y+0z \\\\ (-3)x+8y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140366-a",
