    "q-97031": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97031",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
